Assembler Version 08
====================
Assembled by: version 07 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 07, plus .include directive, file I/O, file stack,
and an expanded instruction set:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch (~label) syntax (also auto-detected via flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection
- Zero page addressing with plain hex values
- .include directive for including external files

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file at current position

Instruction set (expanded from version 07):
  Same as version 06/07, plus:
  CPXZ, CPYZ, DEY, LDXZ, LDYZ, STXZ, STYZ

Error handling: same errors as version 07 (errors 1-A), plus:
- Unknown directive (error B)
- Filename expected (error C)
- No file open (error E): attempt to read with no file open
- Error messages now include filename when inside an included file
- Format: "Error N in file F at line M: message"

New in this version (relative to version 07):
- .include directive: includes contents of another assembly file
- File stack: saves/restores file handle, line number, and filename when
  entering/leaving included files
- File I/O via emulator: open ($F012), close ($F015), read from file ($F018)
- read_char function replaces read_b, reading from current file handle and
  automatically popping the file stack when a file ends
- Null file handle check in read_char: detects attempt to read when no file
  is open and raises error
- Recursive file inclusion support (file stack grows downward from $F000)
- Error messages include current filename when inside an included file
- compare_token helper function extracted for string comparison
- Directive processing: lines starting with . are dispatched to process_directive
- New instructions: CPXZ, CPYZ, DEY, LDXZ, LDYZ, STXZ, STYZ
- Hash table moved: LHASHTABL at $1F00, LHASHTABH at $1F80

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
